Changelog — FCI OTA Request Assistant
All changes documented in reverse chronological order.
---
v1 — June 2026
Initial version
`content_ota_list.js`: Passive listing page automation — opens the first
pending row's Review link (CBO prefix safety check).
`content.js`: Single-stage review page script:
Safety check: Request ID must start with CBO
Clicks "View Action History" and waits for the action history table to populate
Trigger condition: Last "Dispatched" = MAYURESH KUMAR, next entry =
AMIT KUMAR SINGH (Pending Review, N/A) — same pattern as NOC Stage 1
Reads Employee Number and looks up Cadre via hardcoded table:
RISHIKESH MISHRA (286357) → General
SAMYAK NILKANTH MESHRAM (315595) → Depot
Any other employee number → extension stays silent, no action
Sets row 1's Multiplication Factor dropdown (`#multiplication_factor_1`)
to "1.1", then clicks the header checkbox
(`input[name="select_multiplication_factor"]`) to propagate 1.1 to all
rows and recalculate amounts
Checks all three prerequisite checkboxes (register entries / period
checked / person earned OT)
Builds and fills the dynamic Reviewer Remarks with the standard OTA
sanction template, substituting:
Employee Name (from page)
Designation (from page)
Cadre (from lookup table)
Admissible OTA Hours (from page, kept in HH:MM format, not converted
to decimal)
Safety features:
CBO prefix guard on both scripts
No auto-submission — "Review" button always clicked manually by the officer
Highlight trigger row before acting
Unrecognised employee / no trigger match → extension remains silent,
no action taken
Files added: `manifest.json`, `content.js`, `content_ota_list.js`,
`popup.html`, `CHANGELOG.md`
Known pending items:
Only RISHIKESH MISHRA and SAMYAK NILKANTH MESHRAM are in the cadre
lookup table. New OTA applicants must be added to `CADRE_LOOKUP` in
`content.js`.
Listing page table selector (`table.data-table-main-in` /
`table.dataTable`) not yet verified live — update
`content_ota_list.js` if the extension does not auto-open the first row.
Prerequisite checkbox detection uses text-matching heuristics; verify
on a live request that all three checkboxes are found and checked
correctly.
"Admissible OTA Hours" field reading uses a label-proximity + fallback
line-by-line parser; verify the exact value/format extracted matches
the on-page display (e.g. "48:30").
Google Sheets register write-back (per-employee tab) — discussed as a
"good to have" addition, not yet implemented. To be revisited once the
core stage logic is verified on a live request.
